From 0708e4a5d0b4936a3b89fc83d08d11245eab6d68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Framebuffer feedback: the PS1 loop for the loading trail,
 at render resolution

Screen_BackgroundMotionBlur copies the displayed buffer over the cleared draw
buffer with an opaque SPRT, modulated 128 or 127, and Harry draws over it. On
the GPU that is t5 -> (t5*mod)>>7 per channel with word-0 texels skipped:
identity, or one 5-bit level off, so every pose stays on screen until it has
lost 31 levels. The store ran that loop at a gain of 0.7, which turned the
console's second-long smear into a two-frame ghost, and at 320x224 under a
Harry drawn at window resolution.

- g_PsxFeedbackDamp is 1.0.
- An opaque SPRT that copies a display buffer onto the same buffer-relative
  position samples a 1:1 capture of the display area by gl_FragCoord through
  the hi-res override sampler, with the 5-bit arithmetic in the shader and the
  modulation byte recovered from the vertex colour (GR_FeedbackScreenTexture,
  GR_SetFeedbackScreenSample, u_fbScreen). Nothing is resampled, so the loop
  cannot drift; the VRAM rects are still packed from the same capture for the
  blending readers and as the fallback (g_PsxFeedbackScreen, console FBSCREEN).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XhB6DTaXhErTs7bnFrAEbQ
