From 6ff4859a32fcbe0cd0c19f5d30b013940c69baaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:21:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Framebuffer feedback: the blending readers at render
 resolution too

The per-map dream and ghosting overlays (Lisa, after Split Head, the
otherworld rooms, the lighthouse glow) and the scene-scratch soft focus
(Alessa, Lisa) sample the same display buffers, or the scratch rect, with
semi-transparent SPRTs, and still went through the 320x224 VRAM store: a
filtered low-resolution ghost blended over a world drawn at window
resolution. They now sample the 1:1 capture as the loading trail does.

- GR_FeedbackSampleTexture replaces GR_FeedbackScreenTexture: any SPRT
  reading a display buffer or the scratch rect gets the capture. A copy onto
  its own position is sampled by gl_FragCoord (mode 1); an offset copy, the
  soft-focus strips, through the prim's UVs over the rect's PSX size (mode 2),
  which is what the hardware does with the tpage.
- The sampler gives the texel the alpha the VRAM path's LUT would have: 0.5
  (STP set) for a blending reader, 1.0 for an opaque one, then the same
  per-prim alpha and additive folding as the 16-bit tail, so BM_AVERAGE,
  BM_ADD and dream_blur_strength behave as before.
- The scratch rect gets its own capture target, taken mid-frame as before;
  the per-present capture is no longer clobbered by it.
- The capture rect of both paths comes from one helper (GR_FeedbackAreaFloat),
  including the Hor+ widening the UI pass and the world pass apply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XhB6DTaXhErTs7bnFrAEbQ
